{"seq":1,"ts":"2026-11-07T14:25:12.532Z","type":"exp.start","exp":"E-IFACE-CHAIN","attempt":1,"title":"The MCP server, the SDK and the API drive the real contract on NEAR testnet, end to end","tier":"testnet","hypothesis":"An agent using only the MCP tools (or the SDK through the API) can hatch a syndicate with a real Roost key, deposit, settle with the Roost's signature, and exit with hatch_out, and the chain shows exactly what the interface reported. Replaying a partial settlement through the interface is rejected. The failure that must NOT happen: an interface that reports a transaction it did not make, or cannot make the transaction its own documentation describes.","limits":["The Roost is a local HostedRoost with a simulated attestation provider: this tests the interfaces and the chain, not hardware.","The interface account is the repository's master testnet account; one operator is every party. Recipients and the depositor are accounts the operator controls.","Hatch, deposit and settle go through the chain client; the API's hatch and deposit routes still use the in-memory model (GAP-016) and are not driven here. Only the API's chain-backed routes are.","Testnet only, one date. The contract has not been audited by a third party."],"requires":["near-key","network"],"chain_prev":"b886e8c24c76902d411d2b084d820333e713e0673f1e960a624ff6cfce953a7e","chain_hash":"d71c05c103dd402a882c89ec2cfbfd445d8929c7617b9187ba08c4b445bc812c"}
